From: isoriano1968 <81116077+isoriano1968@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 11:55:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] NNNNN hal offers ZFS pool members as volumes

hald-probe-volume reports a ZFS vdev (e.g. the root pool on a USB disk,
storage.removable true) as volume.fstype zfs, volume.fsusage filesystem,
with volume.ignore false, so desktops (gvfs/nautilus) list "rpool" as a
mountable volume that can never be mounted.  ZFS imports pool members
itself; mark them volume.ignore on any disk.

---
--- a/usr/src/cmd/hal/fdi/policy/10osvendor/20-storage-methods.fdi
+++ b/usr/src/cmd/hal/fdi/policy/10osvendor/20-storage-methods.fdi
@@ -83,6 +83,13 @@
         <merge key="volume.ignore" type="bool">true</merge>
       </match>
 
+      <!-- ZFS pool members (vdevs, e.g. the root pool on a USB disk): -->
+      <!-- ZFS imports them, they are never mounted as a volume, so -->
+      <!-- desktops must not offer them in their volume lists -->
+      <match key="volume.fstype" string="zfs">
+        <merge key="volume.ignore" type="bool">true</merge>
+      </match>
+
       <match key="@block.storage_device:storage.removable" bool="false">
 
         <!-- Should always ignore Apple Bootstrap partitions (it would be -->
